# Unsigned wraps that are deliberate, so a run's output is only about us.
#
# -fsanitize=unsigned-integer-overflow reports defined behaviour, which means
# every hash and every sentinel built by subtraction shows up. Three do:
#
#   Qt's qHash mixes by wrapping on purpose, in a header every container
#   instantiates, so it appears in any target that puts bytes in a QHash.
#
#   ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR and _UNKNOWN are (0ULL - 2) and (0ULL - 1), and
#   the comparison expands the macro at the point of use.
#
#   libstdc++ compares two strings of different lengths by wrapping:
#   _S_compare does difference_type(__n1 - __n2), so comparing "" with any
#   four-character key reports 0 - 4. Every std::string comparison of unequal
#   lengths goes through it, which is every lookup in a std::map keyed on one.
#
# Anything else the check reports is ours to look at.
unsigned-integer-overflow:qhashfunctions.h
unsigned-integer-overflow:imagesizeparser.cpp
unsigned-integer-overflow:basic_string.h
unsigned-integer-overflow:basic_string.tcc
